{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And you shall make its dishes.</b> Scripture calls the mold of the bread a קערה, and Rashi explained: קערותיו — its molds. The mold was made in the shape of the bread, and the bread was made like an open box, breached on its two sides — having a base below and folded upward on this side and that side like walls, and therefore it is called לחם הפנים, the bread of the faces, because it has faces seeing this way and that way. And they would make for it a golden mold and an iron mold: in the iron one it was baked, and when they took it out of the oven they would place it in the golden one until the next day, on the Sabbath, when they arranged it upon the Table. <br><b>And its spoons.</b> These are the bowls in which they placed the frankincense — there were two, for the two handfuls of frankincense that they placed upon the two arrangements, as it is said: ״ונתת על המערכת לבונה״. <br><b>And its tubes.</b> Like hollow half-reeds; their pattern is made of gold, separating bread from bread, so that the air enters between them and they do not spoil. <br><b>And its supports.</b> Like golden pegs standing on the ground and rising high above the Table, corresponding to the height of the bread arrangement, and they are split into six branches, one above the other, and the ends of the tubes between bread and bread rest upon those branches, so that the upper breads do not weigh upon the lower ones and break. And therefore Onkelos translated מנקיותיה — מכילתיה, which means its bearers." "<b>And the Ramban</b>, of blessed memory, explained מנקיותיו as 'its measures,' and said that the verses call just measures מנקיות because they are clean (נקיות) from falsehood and from oppression; and the Targum (Leviticus 19:36) of איפת צדק is מכילן דקשוט. And he said that מכילן in the Aramaic tongue means only 'measures' and not 'bearers,' for מכילתיה in the sense of 'bearers' is nothing but a Hebrew expression, from the language of (Jeremiah 20:9) ״ונלאיתי כלכל״; and the matter of the measure is that there was a mold made for the dough, as the Rabbis, of blessed memory, said: there were three molds there."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {1 "The heading 'והרמב\"ן' is not bolded in the source but is presented as a lemma head introducing Ramban's interpretation; rendered in bold to match the commentary's lemma-head convention."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:04:25.616060049Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}